[Music]  LEED is different from other online  courses because it really gives you a  lot in terms of interaction with your  peers teaching assistants but mostly  with the professors that interaction  with the professor's to me is what  completely sets LEED apart from other  online courses never have I faced an  issue where I wanted to reach out to the  faculty but I was not able to and they  were pretty responsive and kind enough  to answer my questions with elaborate  answers when I got exposed to the  faculty that Stanford is famous for it  was beyond impressive there's a lot of  cases where you had live sessions and  you could obviously communicate that way  but there was also a lot of discussions  in the forums or even one-on-one email  dialogues so you definitely had a lot of  support and you felt pretty connected to  and engaged and committed to the classes  you have access to this information and  also this exchange is in such enriching  experiences that any other program did  not experience often I've actually used  case studies or questions that I got the  day before or that I saw the day before  in the lead program and then I would  come across something at work and I  could immediately apply it the courses  are designed such that they give you the  right tools techniques and framework  which you can take and apply in your  career you can do it at your own pace at  your own convenient time LEED is  probably the best learning experience  they can get outside an MBA they're  interested in learning about business  and leadership practices it's not so  much about the the certificate or the  degree it's much about the skills that  are kawaii here

